# LF everywhere: in the repository AND in every working tree, whatever the OS or the
# user's core.autocrlf. Without this, a Windows checkout with autocrlf=true got CRLF
# files, and code that anchors on '\n' over its own source quietly found nothing —
# scripts/sync-dark-palette.mjs threw "no mirror block" on a file that had one, and
# two source-sweep tests failed (tests/helpers/source.ts `readSource` still guards
# those, for checkouts made before this file existed).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touch these, even if one ever looks like text to Git's heuristic.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.onnx binary
*.wasm binary
